  "defaultMode": "light",
  "radius": 20,
  "accent": {
    "_note": "Hako's one accent is asagi (浅葱), the blue-green of Japanese dyed cloth: Kawase's grammar (a fill with a black label, only for the moment that matters: selected controls, the focus ring, badges, the mark's lid) with Hako's own hue. Chosen against the contrast check: the hue must carry a black label (luminance ≥ 0.175) and still read as a focus ring on a white card (≥ 3:1), and it must not sit in the red/amber/green families Senryo already uses for destructive, down, warn and up, nor in Kawase's magenta, MoonPay's purple or the blues of Base and the old brand. Ratios are recorded in .lanes/w04-a-brand.md and printed by check-contrast.mjs.",
    "name": "asagi",
    "kanji": "浅葱",
    "value": "#009CA8"
  },
